## The plan

4 arm(s) x 3 replicates = 12 sweep processes, cache mode fresh, config device NVIDIA H200
EVERYTHING IS SAVED TO  /workspace/results/gaps-nvidia_h200/replicate_noise_floor/nvidia_h200-fresh-n3

MDE: at the assumed sigma 0.0229 this plan resolves 0.0694 in alpha with N=3 replicates per condition, and 0.0906 at the one-run design the study published.
     the sigma is ASSUMED, not measured here: s3-vs-s4 paired sd 0.0323 over 11 cells / sqrt(2). CONFOUNDS num_stages with rerun noise, so it is an upper bound on SAME-SESSION rerun noise and on nothing else: both arms ran in the same pod hour (/workspace/session/20260901T214218Z), so it is NOT established for cross-pod, cross-day or cross-card comparisons. It is also heteroscedastic: mixtral n=4 sd 0.0486 against qwen2 n=7 sd 0.0186, a 2.61x ratio, so it must not be quoted per cell at mixtral G>=8
     it is heteroscedastic by model (mixtral-8x7b 0.0486, qwen2-57b-a14b 0.0186), so a per-cell comparison at mixtral G>=8 is against a wider spread than the pool.
     swizzle swing on mixtral-8x7b is 0.3855, ABOVE the limit, so this design can see it.
     swizzle swing on qwen2-57b-a14b is 0.0226, BELOW the limit: this design CANNOT see it, and the gate for it is registered as an expected FAIL.

INTERLEAVED. The two swizzles of one model run back to back inside a replicate, so their contrast is paired within minutes rather than across blocks:
  order: mixtral-8x7b g1,g16,g16,g1,g1,g16   [counterbalanced]
  order: qwen2-57b-a14b g1,g16,g16,g1,g1,g16   [counterbalanced]

